{"title":"2018 CSMC Problems/Part B Problem 1 Part B","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_1\" title=\"2018 CSMC Problems/Part B Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Alexandra draws a letter A which stands on the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />-axis.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_1_Part_B&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The right side of the letter A lies along the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/e/35edf96252eba7402bbd237547e8ce10796778d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L_{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"22\" height=\"17\" /> and the letter is symmetric about the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />-axis. What is the equation of line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/e/35edf96252eba7402bbd237547e8ce10796778d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L_{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"22\" height=\"17\" />?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_1_Part_B&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The letter is symmetric about the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />-axis, so the sign of the slope of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/e/35edf96252eba7402bbd237547e8ce10796778d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L_{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"22\" height=\"17\" /> must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/e/bae5aba07d37ff6ff813107e76260fb31ad5794e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" /> times the slope of the other line forming the letter. The equation of the other line was <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/9/2a9be1b210be4a436afff9b1354dd77fc24e91a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = 3x + 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"86\" height=\"17\" /> based on <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_1_Part_A\" title=\"2018 CSMC Problems/Part B Problem 1 Part A\">part a</a>, so the equation of line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/e/35edf96252eba7402bbd237547e8ce10796778d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L_{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"22\" height=\"17\" /> must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/e/16e7e06238bc32eb5cff8f1c340a2664b7939bea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{y = -3x + 6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"112\" height=\"29\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018062033\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.013 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.018 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 46/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 165/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 1756/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    7.193      1 2018_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_1\n100.00%    7.193      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:37287:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018062033 and revision id 287933. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}